{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
  "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Six years ago this Court rejected the Navajo Nation's claim for damages in connection with the same action that is before the Court here, the Secretary's approval of amendments to the tribe's mineral lease in the mid-1980s. The Court held there that in order for the United States to be held liable under the Tucker Act or the Indian Tucker Act, the claimant must specify at the threshold a specific rights-creating or duty-imposing statutory or regulatory prescription that the government has allegedly violated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But the question presented, General Kneedler, was limited to IMLA, to the Mineral Leasing Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Tucker Act and the Indian Tucker Act provide that the United States may be liable only for a violation of an act of Congress or a regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Carter G. Phillips)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Absolutely, it's applicable to mineral leases. The -- the language of the statute is \"business leases, including those for the development of mineral resources.\" So clearly it applies to Indian mineral leases, but --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Carter G. Phillips)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the language of the statute is \"business leases, including those for the development of mineral resources.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But your -- your argument is that simply because there isn't that kind of an exclusion in (a), there must have been an intent to permit liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: So did you, Mr. Phillips. Last time around you acknowledged that the Peabody lease was governed only by IMLA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we thought it was in fact an IMLA lease, but in truth --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You bring in Federal officials to testify years after the fact as to what basis they acted earlier? That's very strange to me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: It was after the first time around."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court ought to allow the damages action to go forward."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GEN. KNEEDLER: First, Mr. Chief Justice, with respect to the text of section 5, it doesn't -- it doesn't by any means suggest that it covers mineral leases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1410",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e6d0e6b0a78097975c36d73dd11f35b0a115cae9a2b51e28c78fafbac6d114c6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e6d0e6b0a780-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no further questions --\nCHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, general,\nthe case is submitted."
    },
    {
